# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets headers. See references/connective-tissue.md.

# Hashed build assets - cache hard, forever.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# API routes - never cache.
/api/*
  Cache-Control: no-store

# Security headers for every response.
# X-Frame-Options is SAMEORIGIN (not DENY) so the same-origin Sanity
# Presentation preview iframe still works; cross-origin framing stays blocked.
# WHY script-src CARRIES 'unsafe-inline', measured rather than assumed. A build of this
# template ships three inline scripts: the JSON-LD block, the Vercel adapter's web-analytics
# bootstrap (astro.config.mjs webAnalytics), and any component script Astro decides to inline
# (it inlined ContactForm's validation, and left Motion's as a module). Under a strict policy
# the form validation and the analytics both stop, silently. Hashes cannot fix it here: Vercel
# reads vercel.json from the REPOSITORY rather than from build output, so a hash would have to
# be committed by hand and would go stale the next time anyone edits a component script, which
# kills the script with no error anywhere. So inline script is allowed and the policy is
# honest about what it buys: an injected <script src> from an unlisted host is blocked, so is
# a form posting to another origin, a <base> rewrite, an <object>, and framing by a stranger.
# It does not stop injected inline script.
#
# NEVER add a hash or a nonce to script-src while 'unsafe-inline' is there. A browser that
# sees either one IGNORES 'unsafe-inline', and every inlined script in the build stops running.
#
# The CSP lists the hosts this template actually loads in a browser and nothing else:
# Humblytics (the analytics script, with its own subdomains allowed to connect because the
# beacon endpoint is not knowable from the template) and Cloudflare Turnstile, which also
# needs frame-src because it renders in an iframe. Resend is a SERVER-side fetch from
# src/pages/api/contact.ts and is deliberately absent: widening the policy for a request the
# browser never makes is how a CSP stops describing anything. 'unsafe-inline' is style-src
# only, because Astro inlines small stylesheets; it must never reach script-src.
# Add a host here and in templates/astro-project/vercel.json together, or the two hosts
# disagree about what the same site may load.
#
# HSTS: Vercel sends this itself on a custom domain; Workers does not, so a first request
# over plain http is accepted unless this is here. Two years, subdomains included, and
# deliberately without `preload`, which is a one-way door for a client's apex domain.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://app.humblytics.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.humblytics.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self' data:
